  "description": "This retained revision uses E847-E84A, which overlaps native roughness/reference arrays on its exact supported image. Detection/removal only; use launch_control_v16_ms411. MS41.1 Launch Control V14 retains the native fuel stage, independent fuel thresholds/hysteresis and ignition-cut requests. Fuel-cut ignition angle remains a separate control with its existing episode/recovery behavior. Ignition mode adds LC_RETARD_RANGE and LC_CUT_IGN_ANGLE, evaluated by the required Ignition Cut V14 shared timing owner. The configured RPM region applies on rising and falling RPM, independently of ignition-cut hysteresis, without extending below its lower bound. The optional angle defaults Off; an erased range initializes to 192 RPM. The existing launch input, speed/throttle release and native protective conditions still apply. A revision marker occupies unreachable existing soft-wrapper padding.",
